<header class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="page-head__title">How to build a Canlander deck</h1>
    <p class="page-head__lede">Building a deck mostly comes down to three things: what you spend your ten points on, how the deck wins, and how to get a hundred one-ofs to work together.</p>
    <div class="callout">
      <p class="callout__title">Building your first deck? Start with someone else's.</p>
      <p>Canlander is a hard format to brew for. The points, a hundred singletons and a fast metagame all pull in different directions, and proven lists have already worked that out. Pick a list you like from the <a href="/decks/">deck rotation</a>, the <a href="https://moxfield.com/users/CanlanderWinnersArchive">Winner's Archive</a> or <a href="https://canlandex.com/">Canlandex</a>, play it for a while, then make it your own. This guide explains why those lists look the way they do.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

