    <section id="points" class="docs__section">
      <p class="docs__num mono">01</p>
      <h2>Spend your ten points</h2>
      <p>Before picking cards, think about what your deck needs most from its points. It's usually one of these:</p>
      <dl class="rules-table">
        <div><dt>Raw power</dt><dd>Cards that are simply better than anything else at their job. Black Lotus, Time Walk, Ancestral Recall, the Moxen, Mana Crypt.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Consistency</dt><dd>Tutors that turn your deck into a smaller, more predictable one. Demonic, Vampiric, Mystical and Enlightened Tutor, Imperial Seal, Merchant Scroll.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>An engine</dt><dd>The single card your combo is built around. Flash, Time Vault, Underworld Breach, Tinker, Tolarian Academy, Thassa's Oracle.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>Every competitive deck spends all ten points, so the question is what to spend them on. A combo deck spends on its engine and the tutors to find it. Midrange usually wants raw power it can cast early. Aggro spends on fast mana and cheap pointed threats that let it curve out a turn ahead.</p>

      <h3>Five ways to spend ten</h3>
      <p>See them in action in the <a href="/decks/">deck rotation</a>.</p>
      <div class="spends">
        <div class="spend">
          <p class="spend__name">The Mox package</p>
          <p class="spend__math mono">Mox Emerald 3 · Mox Jet 3 · Mox Ruby 3 · Reanimate 1</p>
          <p>Three free mana sources in your colours. Explosive openings and a lot of turn-two four-drops. Great for decks that want to get ahead early.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spend">
          <p class="spend__name">One bomb, then change</p>
          <p class="spend__math mono">Ancestral Recall 8 · Tamiyo 1 · Psychic Frog 1</p>
          <p>Probably the best draw spell ever printed, plus two cheap threats. You could also do Time Walk at five with five one-pointers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spend">
          <p class="spend__name">The engine and its tutors</p>
          <p class="spend__math mono">Flash 7 · Vampiric Tutor 2 · Imperial Seal 1</p>
          <p>Flash Hulk spends almost everything on the combo piece and a couple of tutors to find it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spend">
          <p class="spend__name">Artifact acceleration</p>
          <p class="spend__math mono">Mana Crypt 5 · Sol Ring 3 · Ancient Tomb 1 · Strip Mine 1</p>
          <p>Ramp straight into large threats a turn or two early. Gruul and colourless decks love this.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spend">
          <p class="spend__name">Spread the ones</p>
          <p class="spend__math mono">Sol Ring 3 · Mox Pearl 3 · Ancient Tomb · Urza's Saga · Strip Mine · White Plume Adventurer</p>
          <p>Two fast mana pieces and four strong one-pointers, so more of your draws are great ones.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Two questions to ask about every pointed card</h3>
      <p><b>What does it do when I draw it on turn six?</b> Black Lotus and the Moxen shine in the first few turns. Tutors and card advantage are great all game. Spend on the cards that are strongest when your deck needs them.</p>
      <p><b>Would I play it if it cost zero?</b> Spend your points on cards that pull their weight in your deck.</p>
